  "result": "The 60-minute lesson on O3, the quiz, its key and a cheat sheet are written. I haven't opened the lesson in a browser. I also couldn't run a word count, so the length is estimated from my section plan (about 6,000–6,500 words, within the 5,400–13,500 range for 60 minutes).\n\n- **Lesson:** `lessons/0001-context-and-memory.html` covers four parts:\n  - The context window and tokens.\n  - What the loop keeps between steps, with a token-cost worked example and a short Python loop.\n  - Context management and notes between sessions.\n  - Retrieval (chunking, keyword versus embedding search, cosine similarity with a worked example), ending with a design exercise for the makerspace assistant.\n- **Quiz:** `quizzes/0002.json` has five items on O3, with the key in `keys/0002.json`. I haven't put any answers here. Ask when you want to take it.\n- **Cheat sheet:** `cheatsheets/context-and-memory.html`.\n- **Workspace:** I added `RESOURCES.md` and updated `NOTES.md`.\n\n**Caveat on sources:** The search results gave only partial text for Anthropic's articles and docs. I limited my claims to what those results supported and cited the pages. One point from a third-party write-up is marked in the lesson as unverified.\n\n**Open question:** I found no community link I could verify, so the lesson lists none. Do you want me to search for one?\n\nAsk me about any part of the lesson.",
